WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:07.570
The world is an unpredictable place. That's
what makes it so haunting when you watch a

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.340
movie years after it's come out, and you realize
that the filmmakers unintentionally predicted

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.680
real-world tragedies. You'll never be able
to watch these movies the same way again.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.320
Game Of Death

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:25.160
Game of Death was released in 1978, five years
after its lead actor, Bruce Lee, had died.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.180
But the completed movie, which was rewritten
after Lee died of unrelated medical complications

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:36.089
during the production, contains a truly eerie
plot point. Lee plays Billy Lo, an actor who's

00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:41.100
shot with a prop gun that turns out to have
a real bullet in it. The shot isn't fatal,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.469
but Lo fakes his death to take revenge on
the would-be assassins.

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:51.120
In 1993, Bruce Lee's son, Brandon Lee, died
while filming The Crow. An actor was supposed

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.670
to fire an unloaded gun at Brandon, but a
bullet fragment that was previously stuck

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.870
in the barrel dislodged while shooting the
blank cartridge. It struck Brandon with same

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.330
velocity as a real round. Brandon Lee died
under nearly the same circumstances depicted

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.080
in his father's final movie.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.210
Demolition Man

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:17.420
Demolition Man from 1993 predicted a high
profile murder nearly a decade before it happened.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.900
The sci-fi film involved a "cryo-prison" where
criminals are frozen and put in cold storage.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:26.730
At one point in the movie, the prisoners who
are frozen with Stallone's character and the

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:32.790
criminal he caught appear on a jailhouse monitor.
One of the names that pops up is "Scott Peterson"—a

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:36.840
name probably chosen by an intern or low level
production assistant

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.410
Fewer than ten years later, in 2002, a woman
named Laci Peterson was brutally murdered

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:49.320
by her husband: Scott Peterson. He was convicted
of killing Laci and their unborn son in 2004,

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.110
and was sentenced to death a year later. In
the years after his conviction and sentencing,

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.830
he was a death row inmate in California's
San Quentin prison. Meanwhile, the cryo-prison

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:05.370
in Demolition Man was where California kept
their worst prisoners—their death row inmates.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.690
The Matrix

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:13.020
To say the prop designer on the set of The
Matrix from 1999 may have inadvertently predicted

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.650
the worst act of terror inflicted on the United
States of America is both unnerving and, more

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:23.220
importantly, not meant to show disrespect
to any of the fallen. However, when watching

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:28.060
the movie now, it's difficult to ignore the
expiration date on Thomas "Neo" Anderson's

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.050
passport, which is 9/11/01.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.170
Poltergeist

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.620
Poltergeist is spooky enough, but it doesn't
end there. The children's room includes a

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:44.230
fake Superbowl 22 poster, which would be
happening in 1988, six years after the movie

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.310
debuted in theaters. Weirdly enough, that
poster inadvertently predicted when Heather

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.900
O'Rourke, the child star who's abducted by
ghosts in the movie, would become fatally

00:02:53.900 --> 00:03:00.680
sick. As Superbowl 22 came around on January
31, 1988, O'Rourke fell violently ill before

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:07.560
passing away the next day due to a cardiac
arrest triggered by an intestinal stenosis.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.650
World's Greatest Dad

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.290
In 2009's World's Greatest Dad, Robin Williams
plays Lance Clayton, a dad and English teacher

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:21.380
whose teenage son accidentally dies from autoerotic
asphyxiation. Clayton, not wanting the police

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.900
or anyone else to find his son's body like
that, makes it look like a suicide instead.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.130
Williams' portrayal of Clayton, combined with
his heartfelt characters who dealt with suicide

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:36.459
in What Dreams May Come, Patch Adams, and
Dead Poets Society, makes his tragic suicide

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:39.370
in 2014 stand out even more.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:43.650
Thanks for watching. Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.290
you just saw.

